  Okay, that's what I thought you were going for.  So my second translation
of "lo nu mi gansu kei na selki'u no da" is what your intended meaning.
 "My action is not justified by nothing" (i.e. -> "lo nu mi  gansu kei
selki'u su'o da" (my action is justified by something))  The discomfort
that I have with the negativity being  part of the brivla instead of within
the arguments is thinking "okay, what would 'lo broda cu tolselki'u lo
brode' mean?" lo broda is justified by something, but not by brode?  If so,
why not simply write "lo broda cu selki'u na'e bo lo brode" or even
simpler, "lo broda na selki'u lo broda"?   It just doesn't feel to me
(pe'i) that "krinu" has a polar opposite in the same way that say "canci"
or "banli" does.  It's not on any kind of scale -- A is either a reason for
B, or it's not.

            --gejyspa


